It't a matter of good interface design.  There are lots of pieces of
equipment that have numerical readouts AND alarms or other indicators
that go off when critical situation arise.  People have a limited
scope of attention.  It's important to have the most important
information the most appearant.  It's very difficult and almost never
done right the first time.  It just seems to require a lot of trial
and error.

A good example is "idiot lights" on cars.  Most people are looking at
the road.  If you expected them to also attend to guages there would
be more accidents or siezed engines.


